WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.480
Within the realm or ports and protocols are
two email protocols to know for the exam:

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:14.040
SMTP or Simple Mail Transfer Protocol and
IMAP, Internet Message Access Protocol.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:21.720
SMTP is an outgoing mail protocol that runs
on port 25, and IMAP is an incoming email

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.760
protocol that runs on port 143.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:30.280
With IMAP, email accessed on a client device
through an app such as Outlook stays on the

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:36.300
email server on which it resides, as opposed
to Post Office Protocol, POP3, which, by default,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.110
would download email off a server and onto
a client device.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:46.670
With the advent of people using multiple devices
to access email, email must stay in one location.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:51.850
Thus, IMAP is in use far more than POP3 for
an incoming email protocol.

